{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N1"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 129, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 3 when edge 4 is also absent leaves only edge 5 feeding the output, causing collapse (exps 4, 6)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "In skip-heavy cells the edge-3 residual is redundant, so removing it hurts less or helps (exp 9)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on edge 5 helps much more when the cell is conv-poor (exps 16, 19)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "With a parameter-free 1->3 edge, a conv on edge 0 adds the only learnable op on that path (exps 28, 29)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the input-output skip, a skip on edge 4 restores a residual path (exp 34)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 1 provides an indirect identity route when edge 3 is missing (exps 57, 58)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 5 when edge 4 is absent nearly disconnects the output from learned features (exps 63, 64)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv costs far more than deleting a skip or pool (exps 61-64 vs 65, 66, 69)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling a missing input-output edge adds a path instead of replacing an existing one (exps 71, 75, 78 vs 72-74)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_